{"step_index":143,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T18:37:03Z","content":"Report updated. Here's the summary:\n\n### @NeonMan — Key Numbers\n\n| Metric | NexLev Says | Realistic Estimate |\n|--------|------------|-------------------|\n| **Monthly Revenue** | \\$15,144 | **~\\$3,500-7,000** |\n| **RPM** | \\$1.72 | **~\\$0.40-0.80** |\n| **Lifetime** | ~\\$2M | **~\\$400K-1.2M** |\n| **Monthly Views** | 8.8M | ✅ (this is real) |\n\n### 🚨 Your Suspicion = CONFIRMED x2\n\nNeonMan is a **pure Hindi gossip channel** about Samay Raina and Indian comedians. NexLev says **40.3% US traffic**. That's as absurd as FactTechz's 45.8%.\n\nThree Hindi channels → same ~40% US, ~22% India pattern. Clearly a **default template**, not real data.\n\n**Bottom line**: NexLev's view counts and category data are solid. Their RPM/revenue/geography for Hindi channels? Take it with a massive grain of salt — actual revenue is probably **3-5x lower** than what NexLev reports for Hindi channels."}
