{"step_index":145,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T18:52:33Z","content":"Good idea — let me first check if NexLev has any tool that accepts custom geographic input, then I'll do the math either way.","thinking":"The user wants me to check if NexLev has a tool that lets me specify custom geographic distributions to calculate RPM/revenue. They want to test:\n1. A realistic estimate (e.g., 70% India, rest distributed)\n2. 95% India + 5% other countries\n\nThe idea is to see if NexLev's RPM calculation changes based on geographic input, or if it always returns the same number regardless.\n\nBut NexLev's `get_geography_revenue` tool only takes a `channelId` as input — there's no way to pass custom geographic distributions. The tool returns fixed estimates for a given channel.\n\nHowever, I can look at what other NexLev tools are available. \n\nChecking the skill's tool list, I see options like youtube_channel_about, get_geography_revenue, and check_channel, but none of them appear to accept a custom geographic breakdown as input.\n\nSo I'll need to approach this differently — using the actual RPM and demographic data NexLev returns, I can mathematically compute what revenue would look like under a different geographic mix, since NexLev doesn't expose per-country RPM directly.\n\nTrying to reverse-engineer per-country RPMs from NexLev's blended $1.72 leaves too many unknowns with five countries and one equation, so instead I'll fall back on known industry-average RPMs for this content category and apply them directly to a hypothetical 95% India distribution.\n\nWorking through the math, this converges to $2.00, matching the category RPM rather than the actual channel RPM of $1.72 -- so the gap likely stems from factors beyond geography, like engagement or ad fill rate, rather than country mix alone. Rather than keep guessing, I should just check whether NexLev's MCP tool schemas expose any geographic input parameters directly.","tool_calls":[{"name":"find_by_name","args":{"Pattern":"*nexlev*","SearchDirectory":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp","toolAction":"Finding NexLev schemas","toolSummary":"NexLev MCP tools"}}]}
